the world is looking to shift to  electric cars and reduce co2 emissions  in transport  to feed this new demand electric vehicle  battery technology is developing rapidly  but with many different solutions new  safety issues arise and for regulators  it can be hard to set the line between  innovation and safety  could we help them to access harmonized  testing data from different sources to  make better and faster regulatory  decisions  we developed new tests addressing  potential safety issues in modern  batteries to help shape regulation  worldwide  our team started by analyzing existing  laws and testing procedures across  countries so that we could address gaps  in regulation  because a vehicle battery catching fire  can be so destructive we're developing a  new test on thermal propagation based on  our research on the many ways such a  reaction could be triggered  once the complete process is validated  in experiments we can propose that it  becomes part of laws to make vehicles  safer  in 2018 our researchers work on  assessing the toxicity of battery  electrolytes resulted in a new global  legal requirement for electric vehicle  safety  this updated global regulation is  expected to include the new thermal  propagation test  with better harmonized test procedures  and global regulation  the jrc and its partners are  facilitating the development of safer  electric vehicles for a sustainable low  carbon world  [Music]
 

